    "description": "KAPS is a dual-pipeline system in Alberta designed to transport natural gas liquids and condensate from the Karr area to Keyera's processing and fractionation network. Its customers are upstream producers and downstream infrastructure users that require contracted liquids takeaway and connectivity into the basin's gathering and processing system. The project is an asset-heavy midstream business with revenue tied to pipeline transportation rather than commodity merchandising. Public sources describe roughly 560 kilometres of pipeline and planned throughput capacity of up to 350,000 barrels per day on the NGL line. Stonepeak agreed to acquire a 50% interest in the project in December 2022, the transaction closed in April 2023, and Keyera continues to operate the system.",
